        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "f3b97cff-4dd1-5888-a265-9077eb54f025",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Gotthold Schwarz, Alexandra Röseler, Heike Kumlin, Martin Krumbiegel, Johann Sebastian Bach\n- Organizations: Thomanerchor, Gewandhausorchester\n- Places: Leipzig\n- Roles: bass-baritone, alto\n- Works: O heilges Geist- und Wasserbad, BWV 165\n\nFacts:\n- Gotthold Schwarz is based in Leipzig.\n- Gotthold Schwarz started as a member of the Thomanerchor.\n- Gotthold Schwarz has conducted the Gewandhausorchester.\n- A bass-baritone is a high-lying bass or low-lying classical baritone voice type that shares certain qualities with the true baritone voice.\n- In 2003, Alexandra Röseler recorded Johann Sebastian Bach's cantata O heilges Geist- und Wasserbad, BWV 165.\n- In the 2003 recording of O heilges Geist- und Wasserbad, BWV 165, Alexandra Röseler sang the alto part.\n- The 2003 recording of O heilges Geist- und Wasserbad, BWV 165 featured Gotthold Schwarz, the Thomanerchor, the Gewandhausorchester, Heike Kumlin, and Martin Krumbiegel.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "d7e5078b-734c-58f5-bf37-e9bf17207072",
        "text": "Page: Gotthold Schwarz. Sentence: Based in Leipzig, he started as a member of the Thomanerchor and has conducted the Gewandhausorchester.\nPage: Bass-baritone. Sentence: A bass-baritone is a high-lying bass or low-lying \"classical\" baritone voice type which shares certain qualities with the true baritone voice.\nPage: Alexandra Röseler. Sentence: In 2003 she recorded Bach's cantata, \"O heilges Geist- und Wasserbad\", BWV 165, with Gotthold Schwarz, Thomanerchor, Gewandhausorchester, Heike Kumlin  and Martin Krumbiegel, singing the alto part.",
